{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"01ee52a7-d622-4ccc-9d48-354184124ff4","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have successfully completed `lab-16-dfs`.\n\nHere is a summary of the actions taken:\n- Examined the syllabus notes (L07c) to integrate relevant vocabulary and concepts into the lab.\n- Created `raid5.py`, a RAID-5 simulator for generating parity bytes and reconstructing missing disks.\n- Created `lfs.py`, a log-structured store showing append operations, indexing, and cleaning (garbage collection).\n- Created `fuse_cache.c` using `libfuse3` in C, because the required `libfuse.so.2` for `fusepy` was missing from the Ubuntu 24.04 VM. It correctly implements a write-back cache, deferring actual disk writes to flush/release time.\n- Configured a `Makefile` supporting `all`, `run`, `test`, and `clean`, verifying everything inside the VM environment through `run-in-vm.sh`.\n- Captured `expected-output.txt` natively inside the VM.\n- Set the seed `README.md` to `status: solid`, populating the goal, prerequisites, run commands, observable outcomes, operational insights, experiments, and questions formatting strictly to vault rules.\n- Committed all files in the designated directory via Git with a conventional message.\n- Output the required completion report to the supervisor's runner path.\n","duration_seconds":316.785451,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":204763,"output_tokens":25594,"thinking_tokens":10429,"cache_read_tokens":2056841,"total_tokens":230357}}}
